WEBVTT

00:01.940 --> 00:04.200
H-Hold it right there!

00:04.820 --> 00:06.830
Where are you taking me?

00:06.830 --> 00:07.950
That way.

00:08.830 --> 00:13.400
How many zombies <i>are</i> there 
in this flock... swarm... pack?!

00:13.400 --> 00:14.400
Dunno.

00:14.400 --> 00:15.830
I've never counted.

00:15.830 --> 00:17.430
They used to be people, right?

00:17.430 --> 00:20.200
And they turned into zombies after 7G?

00:20.200 --> 00:20.950
Who knows?

00:20.950 --> 00:22.660
"Who knows"?!

00:22.660 --> 00:23.950
What are they going to do with me?

00:23.950 --> 00:25.010
Eat you...

00:25.010 --> 00:25.750
What?!

00:25.750 --> 00:27.780
I think? I mean, they're zombies.

00:27.780 --> 00:28.900
The heck?!

00:28.900 --> 00:30.550
I saw you eating canned food!

00:30.550 --> 00:31.750
That doesn't seem right to me!

00:31.750 --> 00:34.600
I can't provide for every last zombie here.

00:34.600 --> 00:36.310
You're the queen, aren't you?!

00:36.310 --> 00:38.240
At least keep your subjects under control!

00:38.240 --> 00:40.540
Also, my panties are going 
to be in full view here!

00:40.310 --> 00:41.140
<i>Panties...</i>

00:40.540 --> 00:41.650
Hey!

00:43.060 --> 00:46.560
If you promise not to run away, 
I'll untie you.

00:46.830 --> 00:47.840
I won't run.

00:47.840 --> 00:48.990
You swear?

00:48.990 --> 00:50.050
I swear!

00:50.780 --> 00:52.210
Untie her.

00:52.210 --> 00:53.690
We'll make her walk.

01:11.340 --> 01:15.090
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

02:27.390 --> 02:28.370
Looks good.

02:28.370 --> 02:30.920
We'll be able to spot it from a distance.

02:31.210 --> 02:33.470
Make sure you stay close by!

02:33.470 --> 02:35.410
Or else you're good as dead!

02:35.410 --> 02:37.110
Yeah, Akira.

02:37.110 --> 02:38.350
You always run off on your own.

02:38.350 --> 02:39.540
I was talking about you!

02:39.540 --> 02:41.060
Okay, let's get going.

02:39.840 --> 02:44.300
Episode 7       A Zombie That Laughs Is No Zombie at All

02:41.060 --> 02:42.440
Off we go!

02:45.170 --> 02:47.650
Wait, how do we find Shizuru-chan?

02:47.650 --> 02:50.070
And what if the zombies already got her?

02:50.070 --> 02:51.750
Zombies come out at night.

02:51.750 --> 02:52.800
Ah.

02:52.800 --> 02:54.440
Zombies have bad eyesight.

02:54.440 --> 02:56.040
Guess that makes sense.

02:56.040 --> 02:57.650
Zombies love brains.

02:57.650 --> 02:58.560
What?

02:58.560 --> 02:59.700
That's why...

02:58.570 --> 03:00.110
<b>Aluminum Foil</b>

03:00.030 --> 03:02.360
You take this, and do this...

03:02.740 --> 03:04.200
and make a fake brain.

03:04.200 --> 03:05.610
What?

03:05.610 --> 03:07.740
Zombies can't resist brains.

03:07.740 --> 03:09.510
If they see a brain, they'll approach it.

03:09.510 --> 03:12.900
So if anything happens, 
throw the brain to buy some time.

03:22.790 --> 03:24.450
That didn't buy us any time!

03:24.450 --> 03:25.960
In fact, it attracted them!

03:25.960 --> 03:27.390
Don't make any sudden movements!

03:27.390 --> 03:27.750
What?!

03:27.750 --> 03:30.650
Zombies can't tell you apart 
if you pretend to be one of them.

03:30.650 --> 03:31.970
Zombies move slowly.

03:32.360 --> 03:34.930
Zombies... don't scream.

03:47.580 --> 03:48.880
They're onto us.

03:48.880 --> 03:50.250
They're totally onto us!

03:50.250 --> 03:51.870
I'll distract them.

03:54.790 --> 03:55.680
Way too close!

03:55.680 --> 03:56.950
Shut up!

03:59.760 --> 04:01.270
Akira-chan, Reimi-chan.

04:01.270 --> 04:02.540
Now's our chance.

04:13.250 --> 04:14.650
Patience. Be patient.

04:14.650 --> 04:17.260
I know, but will this really work?

04:17.260 --> 04:18.820
Zombies don't attack their own.

04:18.820 --> 04:21.740
Yeah, but will paint really fool them...

04:25.110 --> 04:25.960
It did!

04:28.260 --> 04:29.710
Let's move slowly away.

04:29.710 --> 04:30.700
Sounds good.

04:37.600 --> 04:39.130
Is that Shizuru-chan's?

04:43.420 --> 04:45.590
Shizuru-chan's totally a zombie now.

04:45.590 --> 04:47.970
We don't know that for sure.

04:47.970 --> 04:52.270
What if Shizuru-chan can't think 
about anything except eating brains?

04:52.270 --> 04:53.950
Forgetting all about Yoka-chan?

04:53.950 --> 04:55.730
No. That won't happen.

04:55.730 --> 04:56.800
It'll be fine.

05:06.870 --> 05:08.490
A palanquin?

05:08.490 --> 05:09.600
Oh, I see her.

05:09.600 --> 05:10.610
Shizuru-chan's there.

05:10.610 --> 05:11.370
Pochi-san, too.

05:11.370 --> 05:12.540
Turning blue?

05:12.840 --> 05:13.800
Brown.

05:13.800 --> 05:14.630
Brown?

05:14.630 --> 05:16.070
So the rotting's begun?

05:16.070 --> 05:17.440
Nope, fluffy as ever.

05:17.440 --> 05:17.960
Huh?

05:17.960 --> 05:19.120
Pochi-san, right?

05:19.120 --> 05:21.610
No, the human! Shizuru-chan!

05:21.610 --> 05:24.310
Her face looks normal to me.

05:24.310 --> 05:25.290
Yeah, it does.

05:25.290 --> 05:27.930
So she's not a zombie yet?

05:27.930 --> 05:30.670
Then why is she being so obedient?

05:30.670 --> 05:32.920
You'd think she would go and start trouble.

05:32.920 --> 05:34.280
She absolutely would.

05:34.530 --> 05:36.670
Oh, she looks surprised.

05:36.670 --> 05:38.340
She fell down and landed on her butt.

05:38.340 --> 05:39.950
I can see that from here.

05:39.950 --> 05:41.120
Is she saying something?

05:41.120 --> 05:41.970
Hey, Shiz—

05:42.970 --> 05:44.980
We're in zombie mode! Zombie mode!

05:45.660 --> 05:47.300
Huh? Is she itchy?

05:47.300 --> 05:48.580
Has she started to turn?

05:48.580 --> 05:49.360
No.

05:49.360 --> 05:52.120
I think she's asking if we're 
zombies or still human.

05:52.120 --> 05:53.950
Oh, because of our face paint.

05:53.950 --> 05:56.840
Nadeko-chan, you look 
the worst with that azure.

05:56.840 --> 05:57.890
Azure...

05:57.890 --> 05:59.880
It even sounds like a zombie moaning.

05:59.880 --> 06:01.120
Would "sky blue" be better?

06:01.120 --> 06:01.880
What?

06:01.880 --> 06:03.160
Can't move your eyeballs?

06:03.160 --> 06:04.300
Arms about to fall off?

06:04.300 --> 06:05.340
Need more brains?

06:05.340 --> 06:07.520
Oh, no! Oh, no!

06:07.520 --> 06:08.190
What's wrong?

06:10.560 --> 06:12.460
What's with those three?

06:15.000 --> 06:15.800
Hey!

06:16.280 --> 06:19.580
Huh, your ex-human ex-friends?

06:19.580 --> 06:20.340
"Ex"?!

06:20.340 --> 06:21.320
"Friends"?!

06:20.340 --> 06:21.320
"Human"?!

06:21.320 --> 06:23.470
Or are they your human ex-friends?

06:26.210 --> 06:27.440
Or maybe...

06:27.440 --> 06:29.780
Ex-human friends?

06:29.780 --> 06:31.270
Human friends?

06:31.270 --> 06:33.070
Do you really need to sweat the details?

06:33.070 --> 06:34.980
All this ex or not stuff!

06:34.980 --> 06:35.920
Yes, I do!

06:35.920 --> 06:37.900
I won't abide rebellion.

06:37.900 --> 06:41.930
You can still speak, which means either 
you've only just turned into zombies,

06:41.930 --> 06:43.900
or you're just pretending.

06:44.730 --> 06:46.120
Don't feel like answering?

06:47.160 --> 06:48.170
So be it.

06:48.170 --> 06:51.460
Your bodies will tell us 
whether you're really zombies.

06:51.460 --> 06:52.570
Our bodies?!

06:52.570 --> 06:53.020
Hey.

06:53.260 --> 06:54.730
Bring the you-know-what.

06:54.730 --> 06:56.300
An iron maiden?

06:56.300 --> 06:57.380
A brazen bull?

06:57.730 --> 06:59.300
A Judas cradle?

07:02.080 --> 07:03.300
Udon?!

07:03.300 --> 07:04.810
This is no ordinary udon.

07:05.080 --> 07:06.500
It's a Musashino specialty.

07:06.500 --> 07:10.630
Thick noodles simmered in miso 
with seasonal veggies and pork.

07:10.630 --> 07:12.680
A toothsome, country-style udon.

07:13.210 --> 07:15.320
Shake a bit of shichimi pepper on here...

07:20.520 --> 07:24.590
Chew down on the springy noodles 
and slurp the broth,

07:25.210 --> 07:26.840
with bites of pork in between...

07:26.840 --> 07:28.500
Eating all by yourself again?

07:28.870 --> 07:31.370
I'm special because I'm the queen.

07:31.370 --> 07:34.240
Zombies usually don't have any appetite.

07:35.620 --> 07:38.500
You didn't show any reaction 
to the simmered udon.

07:38.500 --> 07:40.130
It looks like you really are zombies.

07:40.130 --> 07:42.280
Uh-huh. We're zombies, all right.

07:42.280 --> 07:44.390
We come in zombie peace.

07:44.390 --> 07:46.850
I still can't say with complete confidence.

08:03.530 --> 08:05.310
Ah, you died again!

08:05.310 --> 08:06.830
You suck.

08:08.340 --> 08:12.760
Even so, I'm the queen, so I don't 
need to let anyone else have a turn.

08:12.760 --> 08:13.710
No.

08:13.710 --> 08:15.490
It's a snap of the wrist to reload...

08:15.490 --> 08:16.440
What was that?

08:17.120 --> 08:18.470
Ah, so frustrating...

08:18.470 --> 08:19.650
Frustrating?

08:19.650 --> 08:21.410
Zombies don't fret.

08:21.410 --> 08:22.890
Thus, they don't get frustrated.

08:22.890 --> 08:24.430
I'm not.

08:24.430 --> 08:25.550
Really?

08:25.550 --> 08:26.780
Wanna try?

08:26.780 --> 08:28.810
I... won't!

08:28.810 --> 08:30.140
Zombies don't play games.

08:30.490 --> 08:33.050
What if the queen commands you to?

08:33.630 --> 08:34.720
Why, you!

08:34.720 --> 08:36.320
Damn it!

08:36.330 --> 08:37.920
Eat this!

08:37.920 --> 08:39.090
Headshot!

08:39.090 --> 08:42.160
Nadeko-chan's like a whole different person 
when she plays games.

08:42.160 --> 08:44.270
And when she holds a bow.

08:44.270 --> 08:46.470
She'd be unstoppable 
if she had a bow in the game.

08:46.470 --> 08:49.090
Die, damn it!

08:49.090 --> 08:50.010
Hell yes!

08:50.010 --> 08:51.290
Stupid zombies!

08:51.290 --> 08:53.130
You're pretty good at this.

08:55.840 --> 08:57.750
All thanks to you.

08:57.750 --> 09:00.550
You have pretty fast reactions for a zombie.

09:02.020 --> 09:03.420
That's because, you know...

09:03.420 --> 09:06.910
She still has her reflexes, 
since she only just turned into a zombie.

09:06.910 --> 09:07.430
Right?

09:07.430 --> 09:08.400
Yes, yes!

09:12.310 --> 09:13.650
Zombies don't laugh.

09:14.990 --> 09:18.000
A zombie that laughs is no zombie at all.

09:18.000 --> 09:19.500
Which means...

09:19.500 --> 09:20.590
Which means?

09:21.330 --> 09:22.580
You're human.

09:24.130 --> 09:25.510
Tie them up!

09:25.880 --> 09:27.050
Stop it!

09:27.360 --> 09:30.170
If you're on their side, 
that makes you an enemy, too!

09:30.170 --> 09:31.900
I'll eat all your brains!

09:31.900 --> 09:32.760
Just try it!

09:40.480 --> 09:42.460
Hi-yah!

09:46.230 --> 09:47.260
Shizuru-chan!

09:47.260 --> 09:48.340
Wow.

09:49.530 --> 09:50.770
Ah, it came off.

09:50.770 --> 09:52.250
Are these guys actually super weak?

09:52.250 --> 09:53.350
Maybe we can win this.

09:55.440 --> 09:57.160
That's amazing, Akira-chan!

09:57.160 --> 10:00.190
She's scared of ghosts, 
but she can handle zombies just fine.

10:00.650 --> 10:02.190
Take this!

10:08.930 --> 10:09.860
We can do this!

10:17.020 --> 10:18.270
How?!

10:21.690 --> 10:22.670
They stuck back together!

10:23.090 --> 10:24.340
What the heck?

10:24.340 --> 10:25.480
Endless zombies!

10:25.480 --> 10:27.030
Zombies don't die.

10:27.030 --> 10:27.830
Not fair!

10:27.830 --> 10:29.520
That's just how their bodily systems work.

10:29.520 --> 10:30.820
Nothing unfair about it.

10:30.820 --> 10:33.680
System? Stim...

10:33.680 --> 10:37.280
<i>We've just received eyewitness 
reports of migratory zombies.</i>

10:37.280 --> 10:39.090
Migratory zombies?

10:39.090 --> 10:41.310
They're a real pain in the neck.

10:41.310 --> 10:43.500
However much you beat them, 
they keep coming back.

10:43.500 --> 10:44.720
They're weak but never die.

10:44.720 --> 10:46.540
How are you supposed to deal with that?

10:48.310 --> 10:51.830
I haven't confirmed it, but it seems 
zombies are weak to stimulation.

10:51.830 --> 10:52.510
Stimulation?

10:52.510 --> 10:55.240
You mean, like, from living things?

10:55.240 --> 10:56.620
They attack humans, don't they?

10:56.620 --> 10:59.570
Well, you shouldn't take it too seriously.

10:59.570 --> 11:00.120
Yep.

11:00.120 --> 11:03.330
Are you talking about sexual 
or erotic stimulation?

11:03.330 --> 11:04.370
Akira-chan!

11:04.370 --> 11:06.550
Ew, are you saying zombies are pervs?

11:06.550 --> 11:09.550
No, they can't handle it. 
It's like their weak point.

11:09.550 --> 11:12.750
Zombies are the very 
personification of death.

11:12.750 --> 11:14.020
Thanatos, as it were.

11:14.020 --> 11:15.900
Yin. Destruction. Annihilation.

11:15.900 --> 11:17.260
Opposite it lies...

11:17.260 --> 11:17.900
Eros.

11:18.720 --> 11:20.830
A mindset that values sensuality.

11:18.720 --> 11:21.740
Akira-chan's going on 
about weird stuff again.

11:20.830 --> 11:25.950
A yearning for beauty, goodness, 
and all living things.

11:21.740 --> 11:22.940
Shh!

11:24.470 --> 11:27.080
I don't know what she's 
talking about anymore.

11:27.080 --> 11:28.530
Are we still talking about zombies?

11:28.530 --> 11:29.850
Be careful.

11:29.850 --> 11:32.110
It's best if you can avoid zombies altogether,

11:32.110 --> 11:34.670
but if they get close, 
the ground rule is to stay still.

11:34.980 --> 11:39.130
What I mentioned is just 
one possible zombie theory.

11:39.660 --> 11:44.170
Erotic!

11:42.540 --> 11:43.630
Nade—

11:44.170 --> 11:45.640
No! You've got it wrong!

11:45.640 --> 11:47.630
You see, we're talking about eroticism!

11:47.630 --> 11:48.770
E-Erotic?!

11:48.770 --> 11:49.390
No!

11:49.390 --> 11:51.510
Um, let's get this straight, Shizuru-chan!

11:51.510 --> 11:53.190
What Neko-nii-san mentioned?

11:53.190 --> 11:54.400
Yeah, that!

11:54.400 --> 11:55.570
Please, Akira-chan!

11:55.570 --> 11:56.770
Say something erotic!

11:57.030 --> 11:57.990
What?!

11:57.990 --> 12:00.080
Anything's fine! Hurry!

12:00.080 --> 12:02.340
Something erotic, something erotic...

12:02.340 --> 12:04.570
I know, that English novel!

12:05.990 --> 12:14.150
"Mellors laid his hand in pure desire, 
stroking the silky slope of her loins."

12:14.570 --> 12:20.290
"His fingers traveled down, 
coming nearer to the very quick of her."

12:20.290 --> 12:24.470
"Connie's resistance was gone, 
left without shame."

12:24.470 --> 12:29.270
"Spreading her lovely thighs, 
she went all open to him."

12:29.770 --> 12:35.220
"She felt his manhood risen against her 
with amazing assertion."

12:35.510 --> 12:36.460
Pervy...

12:36.460 --> 12:37.880
I swear, Akira...

12:39.610 --> 12:41.840
Nadeko-chan, don't be gross!

12:46.390 --> 12:48.160
He's laughing?

12:48.160 --> 12:50.370
I thought zombies didn't laugh.

12:51.410 --> 12:52.540
He exploded!

12:55.010 --> 12:57.140
Akira, you're amazing!

12:57.140 --> 13:00.580
How do they know the zombies' weakness?!

13:11.210 --> 13:12.840
More erotic stuff!

13:12.840 --> 13:14.040
What about grotesque?

13:14.040 --> 13:14.730
Nope!

13:14.730 --> 13:15.850
I'm all out!

13:15.850 --> 13:17.300
Think something up!

13:17.300 --> 13:17.890
No way!

13:17.890 --> 13:19.280
<i>You</i> come up with something!

13:19.280 --> 13:21.300
Something pervy, something pervy...

13:21.300 --> 13:24.150
T... Tw... Th...

13:24.150 --> 13:25.930
Throbbing!

13:25.930 --> 13:27.680
Whoa, that's kinda hot!

13:27.680 --> 13:28.800
H...

13:28.800 --> 13:30.730
Hanky-panky!

13:31.250 --> 13:33.030
Huh? Hanky?

13:33.030 --> 13:34.910
K... C...

13:34.910 --> 13:35.590
Crawling!

13:37.990 --> 13:40.890
Nadeko-chan, crawling doesn't sound dirty!

13:52.500 --> 13:54.820
Ugh, so icky!

13:54.820 --> 13:57.000
It'd sound dirty if you said "sticky."

13:57.000 --> 13:59.220
I guess that might sound naughty to some.

13:59.220 --> 14:00.800
S... S...

14:00.800 --> 14:02.510
Squirming. Is that erotic?

14:02.510 --> 14:03.880
I'm not sure.

14:03.880 --> 14:05.500
Guess it depends?

14:05.500 --> 14:06.180
B...

14:07.260 --> 14:09.020
Bicker, bicker. Yell, yell.

14:09.370 --> 14:10.230
What?

14:10.960 --> 14:12.490
Mope, mope.

14:12.490 --> 14:13.620
Dilly-dally.

14:13.620 --> 14:14.880
Bad, bad.

14:14.880 --> 14:16.010
Worry, worry.

14:16.890 --> 14:19.740
B-Beg, beg.

14:21.910 --> 14:25.480
Shizuru-chan, save that for Yoka-chan.

14:35.830 --> 14:37.680
Our train is here.

14:37.680 --> 14:38.930
Agano's over here.

14:38.440 --> 14:40.020
<b>Ikebukuro</b>

14:38.440 --> 14:41.900
<b>Us</b>

14:38.440 --> 14:41.900
<b>Agano</b>

14:38.440 --> 14:41.900
<b>Sacred Tree</b>

14:38.930 --> 14:40.170
Ikebukuro's that way.

14:40.170 --> 14:41.900
And the zombies are around here.

14:40.350 --> 14:41.900
<b>Ikebukuro</b>

14:41.900 --> 14:42.850
What?

14:42.850 --> 14:44.520
Do we go through the zombies?

14:44.520 --> 14:45.540
With our train?

14:45.540 --> 14:47.540
Grinding and snapping through them?

14:47.540 --> 14:49.430
I kind of... <i>really</i> don't want that.

14:49.430 --> 14:51.040
Oh, yeah. It's almost five.

14:51.040 --> 14:52.490
Time to report to Zenjiro-san.

14:52.760 --> 14:55.190
Zenjiro-san might be able 
to teach us something dirty!

14:55.190 --> 14:57.040
Huh? You can teach us a song?

14:57.040 --> 14:58.050
Awesome!

14:58.050 --> 14:58.830
Nadeko-chan!

14:58.830 --> 15:00.210
I'll dictate, so write it down.

15:00.210 --> 15:00.990
Got it.

15:02.170 --> 15:03.970
Let me sing you a song!

15:19.300 --> 15:20.730
You won't get away.

15:21.250 --> 15:22.870
Zombies, have at them!

15:22.870 --> 15:24.100
Capture the humans!

15:29.000 --> 15:30.830
Ugh, look at <i>that</i>!

15:30.830 --> 15:32.490
What if it doesn't work?

15:32.490 --> 15:34.120
We won't know till we try.

15:40.490 --> 15:43.510
Tonight's a sweaty lovemaking festival!

15:43.510 --> 15:48.500
The lady back home, get her hot, 
strip her, spread her, line her up!

15:48.500 --> 15:51.080
Hey! Get rubbing, thrusting, ram-a-lama!

15:51.080 --> 15:53.620
Wham bam, ram-a-lam, bam ba-bam bam!

15:53.620 --> 15:54.090
And again!

15:54.090 --> 15:56.470
Wham bam, ram-a-lam, bam ba-bam bam!

16:03.790 --> 16:04.730
Really?!

16:05.090 --> 16:06.480
It worked, it worked!

16:06.480 --> 16:08.100
Zenjiro-san's amazing!

16:08.100 --> 16:10.600
I think that's the first time 
he's actually been helpful.

16:14.880 --> 16:16.210
They're not coming here.

16:16.210 --> 16:17.840
What's the big deal?!

16:17.840 --> 16:21.860
Moving in a pack isn't very 
zombie-like to begin with.

16:21.860 --> 16:23.120
Huh? Really?

16:23.120 --> 16:27.850
Well, it means there's a chain of command, 
with a leader and followers.

16:27.850 --> 16:30.770
I didn't know zombies even had a hierarchy.

16:30.770 --> 16:31.970
That's right.

16:31.970 --> 16:34.170
They're taking commands 
from the zombie queen.

16:34.940 --> 16:36.230
Wait, Shizuru-chan!

16:36.230 --> 16:37.150
Where are you going?

16:37.150 --> 16:38.540
Off to talk with the queen.

16:38.540 --> 16:39.280
What?!

16:40.880 --> 16:41.910
Talk with her?

16:41.910 --> 16:43.300
No, you can't!

16:43.300 --> 16:46.000
You think you can talk 
things out with a zombie?

16:46.000 --> 16:48.980
You see, the queen probably isn't a zombie.

16:48.980 --> 16:49.600
Huh?

16:49.880 --> 16:52.430
She was the only one eating real food, right?

16:52.430 --> 16:53.460
Like udon.

16:53.460 --> 16:55.120
Not that she gave us any.

16:55.900 --> 16:58.240
But isn't that because she's the queen?

16:58.240 --> 17:00.250
That's her excuse. I think.

17:00.830 --> 17:03.780
She'd be in trouble 
if they knew she was human.

17:03.780 --> 17:05.130
I guess, yeah.

17:05.130 --> 17:07.240
After she pretended to be their queen.

17:07.240 --> 17:09.000
So use that to threaten her?

17:09.000 --> 17:11.740
What if she really is a real zombie?

17:12.410 --> 17:15.420
If she really is a real zombie, 
I'll fight her.

17:15.420 --> 17:18.310
Not even the queen can come back 
if she's smashed into pieces.

17:18.310 --> 17:19.420
Smashed into pieces?!

17:19.420 --> 17:21.440
Don't mess with Agano jiu-jutsu!

17:21.440 --> 17:22.640
I'll go with you.

17:22.640 --> 17:24.920
You've got your Agano jiu-jitsu,

17:24.920 --> 17:28.600
and I have Agano archery and my 
hours in <i>The House of the Dead</i>!

17:33.760 --> 17:35.990
Hey! We want to talk!

17:35.990 --> 17:36.660
What?

17:40.410 --> 17:41.020
Stop!

17:47.650 --> 17:48.690
Why?

17:49.330 --> 17:50.430
Why what?

17:50.780 --> 17:52.410
Because they'll eat you if they find out?

17:58.850 --> 17:59.980
What?

17:59.980 --> 18:01.140
What happened?

18:01.670 --> 18:03.580
Where'd everyone go?

18:17.020 --> 18:17.980
What?

18:17.980 --> 18:19.150
What's going on?

18:20.730 --> 18:23.080
Oh, no! They can see my panties!

18:24.790 --> 18:27.540
Is it the panties?

18:28.400 --> 18:30.540
You've been their queen ever since?

18:32.050 --> 18:33.760
Pretending you're a zombie?

18:33.760 --> 18:35.250
Reimi-chan!

18:35.250 --> 18:37.810
I didn't want to pretend, 
but I didn't have a choice.

18:38.130 --> 18:40.350
Which station's closest to your house?

18:40.350 --> 18:41.400
Hoya.

18:41.400 --> 18:43.410
You didn't think to go back?

18:43.410 --> 18:45.770
I did, but still...

18:45.770 --> 18:48.160
You couldn't have the zombies find out?

18:48.160 --> 18:51.350
That's true too, but...

18:55.910 --> 18:57.240
Don't move!

19:04.020 --> 19:05.290
I need to go back!

19:39.100 --> 19:40.810
You were waiting for me?

19:49.580 --> 19:51.780
Good job surviving the mold, my subjects!

19:51.780 --> 19:54.000
The queen commends you!

20:00.710 --> 20:02.200
I see...

20:02.200 --> 20:04.120
A master and her servants. How nice!

20:04.120 --> 20:07.350
So you took the zombies with you 
to wander around together.

20:07.350 --> 20:11.490
If I didn't, they'd grow mold 
and fall to pieces.

20:11.490 --> 20:12.390
Makes sense.

20:12.390 --> 20:14.520
I guess you were a pretty nice queen.

20:14.520 --> 20:16.180
I didn't have any other choice.

20:16.180 --> 20:17.410
Nope.

20:17.410 --> 20:18.690
You've been a good queen to them.

20:19.910 --> 20:21.030
Thanks.

20:21.030 --> 20:23.310
We're on our way to Ikebukuro.

20:23.310 --> 20:24.710
How 'bout you, Kurokin?

20:24.710 --> 20:26.260
When'd you get so friendly with her?

20:26.260 --> 20:27.750
It's fine! We're friends!

20:28.040 --> 20:29.290
Friends...

20:29.290 --> 20:32.220
Want to come with us to Ikebukuro, 
Kurokin-chan?

20:32.220 --> 20:35.670
Ikebukuro... with friends...

20:37.520 --> 20:38.760
Together...

20:41.900 --> 20:44.620
I can't do that. I'm the queen.

20:44.620 --> 20:45.660
But, you know...

20:45.660 --> 20:47.250
Sorry for holding you up.

20:48.410 --> 20:52.480
I haven't seen any humans in so long 
that I just wanted to talk.

20:52.480 --> 20:57.260
But if you have somewhere to go, 
I shouldn't be stopping you.

20:58.240 --> 21:01.280
I'll tell the zombies not 
to attack any humans.

21:01.280 --> 21:06.040
You'll still be feared and hated, and you 
might even end up being attacked yourself.

21:06.040 --> 21:07.250
I'm used to it.

21:07.250 --> 21:07.980
What?

21:07.980 --> 21:11.490
But I'm different from how I used to be,

21:11.490 --> 21:13.370
and now I have these zombies here with me.

21:13.370 --> 21:15.690
There's no need for you to worry.

21:15.690 --> 21:16.840
Got it.

21:19.830 --> 21:21.330
Be careful on your journey.

21:21.330 --> 21:24.180
I hear that Ikebukuro has its own queen.

21:24.180 --> 21:25.250
See you later!

21:25.250 --> 21:26.650
We'll stop by on our way back!

21:26.650 --> 21:27.910
Watch your panties!

21:27.910 --> 21:31.140
You can reload with a 
small snap of the wrist!

21:31.140 --> 21:33.250
Good luck beating chapter one!

21:31.990 --> 21:33.970
Be especially careful of the queen!

21:38.060 --> 21:41.230
You think Kurokin was bullied as a kid?

21:41.230 --> 21:42.940
Huh? That doesn't matter!

21:42.940 --> 21:44.140
Sure it does.

21:44.140 --> 21:44.830
What?

21:44.830 --> 21:47.450
The past is linked to who you are now,

21:47.450 --> 21:49.240
as well as who you'll be in the future.

21:49.240 --> 21:51.290
For better or for worse.

21:51.290 --> 21:53.480
For richer, for poorer.

21:53.480 --> 21:54.200
Not quite.

21:54.200 --> 21:55.610
Why not?

21:55.610 --> 21:56.830
Everyone and their dog, then.

21:56.100 --> 21:57.480
Shizuru-chan.

21:56.830 --> 21:57.600
Getting colder.

21:57.600 --> 21:58.160
What?!

21:58.160 --> 21:59.840
How about pearls before swine?

21:59.840 --> 22:00.970
Totally off!

22:00.970 --> 22:02.230
Substance over style?

22:02.230 --> 22:03.470
Not even close!

22:04.340 --> 22:09.970
14 Stops Left Until Ikebukuro

22:04.380 --> 22:05.830
The hunter becomes the hunted?

22:05.830 --> 22:06.540
Nope!
